# FreedomForge Max — Blackbox AI Rules

## Project Identity
This is FreedomForge Max — an autonomous intelligence engine for financial empowerment, tax intelligence, and human-first AI interactions built with Next.js 16, React 19, and TypeScript.

## Architecture
- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript 5
- Styling: Tailwind CSS 4
- AI Backend: OpenRouter multi-model routing (26 MAX + 10 Advisor models)
- Trading Backend: OCI (Oracle Cloud Infrastructure)
- Auth: HMAC-SHA256 sessions
- Testing: Vitest 4.1 (109+ tests)
- Deploy: Railway (https://freedomforge.one)

## File Structure
- app/ — Next.js App Router pages and API routes
- lib/ — Core business logic, models, utilities
- middleware.ts — Edge auth, rate limiting, CSRF
- public/ — PWA assets, service worker

## Critical Files (Handle With Care)
- lib/ucfee-virtues.ts — 5,600+ line behavioral framework (UCFEE-2.0)
- lib/advisor-knowledge.ts — 916 line tax/legal knowledge base
- lib/models.ts — AI model registry
- middleware.ts — Security middleware

## Coding Rules
1. TypeScript strict mode — no `any` types unless unavoidable
2. Tests live next to source files (*.test.ts / *.test.tsx)
3. Run `npm test` before committing
4. All AI API calls go through OpenRouter
5. API routes use SSE (Server-Sent Events) for streaming
6. Environment variables in .env.local (never commit secrets)
7. Follow existing code patterns — check similar files first

